                       "\u003cstrong\u003eTrue shopping cost: about $50.72 across 14 servings, roughly $3.62 per burrito.\u003c/strong\u003e What the register trip looks like if your pantry is already stocked. Meat, produce, and packaged items are counted as the whole packages you have to buy, since you cannot grab a partial box, can, or jar. Pantry staples you already own (rice, seasonings, oils, and long-lasting sauces) are counted at only what this batch uses.",
