    "cost_closing_html":  "\u003cp\u003eThat is about \u003cstrong\u003e${{cost_ps}} a burrito\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost) versus \u003cstrong\u003e$10 or more\u003c/strong\u003e for a build-your-own turkey burrito. The vegetables stretch the turkey, which is how the cost stays down.\u003c/p\u003e",
    "shop_smart":  [
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eGround turkey goes on sale as often as beef.\u003c/strong\u003e Buy the 93/7 when it drops and freeze it in one-pound packs. The leaner grinds cost more for almost no macro gain here, so 93/7 is the sweet spot.",
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eOne sweet potato and one zucchini stretch across the batch.\u003c/strong\u003e They add fiber and bulk for pennies and keep the filling from being just meat and cheese. Dice them small so they cook fast.",
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eA can of chipotle in adobo is your smoky heat for months.\u003c/strong\u003e You blend a few spoonfuls in, then freeze the rest in cubes. Buying a fresh can every time is money down the drain."
                   ],
    "make_it":  [
                    "Weigh your empty mixing pot and write the number down for portioning later.",
                    "Dice the sweet potato, zucchini, red bell pepper, and yellow onion small so they cook quickly.",
                    "Heat the vegetable oil in a large skillet and cook the ground turkey over medium-high heat, breaking it up, until browned.",
                    "Add the diced vegetables, the blended chipotle in adobo, ground cumin, chili powder, and garlic powder, and cook until the vegetables are tender.",
                    "Pour in the chicken broth and the drained black beans and simmer until the liquid cooks down.",
                    "Off the heat, stir in the Greek yogurt, the Mexican cheese blend, and the chopped cilantro so the sauce goes creamy.",
                    "Warm the tortillas so they roll cleanly, then fill and wrap each one."
                ],
